## 4. Formal Interface Contracts

To guarantee that components interoperate seamlessly without brittle coupling, all core modules adhere to strict abstract base classes defined in `quantforge.core.base`:

```python
# Conceptual Interface Contracts

class BaseExperiment(ABC):
    """Abstract lifecycle for all research experiments."""
    @abstractmethod
    def setup(self, config: ExperimentConfig) -> None: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def run(self) -> ExperimentResult: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def validate(self) -> ValidationReport: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def export_artifacts(self, artifact_dir: Path) -> None: ...

class BasePricer(ABC):
    """Abstract interface for derivatives pricing engines."""
    @abstractmethod
    def price(self, instrument: DerivativeInstrument) -> PricingResult: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def greeks(self, instrument: DerivativeInstrument) -> GreeksResult: ...

class BaseBanditPolicy(ABC):
    """Abstract interface for multi-armed and risk-sensitive bandits."""
    @abstractmethod
    def select_arm(self) -> int: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def update(self, arm: int, reward: float) -> None: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def get_regret(self) -> float: ...

class BasePortfolioSolver(ABC):
    """Abstract interface for portfolio optimization."""
    @abstractmethod
    def solve(self, expected_returns: np.ndarray, cov_matrix: np.ndarray,
              constraints: PortfolioConstraints) -> OptimizationResult: ...
```

